As the subject says, I&#39;m trying to embed hrefs in cells of a table.  As far as I can tell, there are two threads on this group that describe approaches:<div><br></div><div>1) write out a table in html in a renderText() function and use htmlOutput() to display</div><div>2) use renderTable() and make sure to redefine the xtable sanitize.text.function() to not escape references.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve tried both and have not been successful. I suspect that I&#39;m just doing something silly, but I&#39;m not sure what it is.  I&#39;ve attached test versions of server.R and ui.R.</div><div><br></div><div>ui.R tries to display three tables, (two that create html code and one that uses renderTable()) but only the first (the one without links) seems to work </div><div><br></div><div>Any advice would be greatly appreciated.</div><div>cheers,</div><div>Allan</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>ui.R</div><div>#################</div><div><div>shinyUI(pageWithSidebar(</div><div>  headerPanel(&quot;HTML output&quot;), </div><div>  sidebarPanel(sliderInput(&quot;n&quot;, </div><div>    &quot;Number of on each side:&quot;, min = 0, max = 10, value = 5)), </div><div>    mainPanel(</div><div>        htmlOutput(&quot;test_table&quot;)</div><div>        ,</div><div>        htmlOutput(&quot;test_table_url&quot;)</div><div>        ,</div><div>        tableOutput(&quot;test_table_url2&quot;)</div><div>        )</div><div>))</div></div><div><br></div><div>server.R</div><div>#########################</div><div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output) {</div><div>    output$test_table &lt;- renderText( {</div><div><br></div><div>        str &lt;- &quot;&lt;table border=1&gt;
&quot;</div><div>        for (i in 1:input$n) {</div><div>          str &lt;- paste(str, &quot;  &lt;tr&gt;
&quot;, sep = &quot;&quot;)</div><div>          str &lt;- paste(str, &quot;    &lt;td&gt;&quot;,i,&quot;&lt;/td&gt;&quot;, sep = &quot;&quot;)</div><div>        }</div><div>        str</div><div>    })</div><div>    </div><div>    output$test_table_url &lt;- renderText( {</div><div><br></div><div>        str &lt;- &quot;&lt;table border=1&gt;
&quot;</div><div>        for (i in 1:input$n) {</div><div>          str &lt;- paste(str, &quot;  &lt;tr&gt;
&quot;, sep = &quot;&quot;)</div><div>          str &lt;- paste(str, &quot;    &lt;td&gt;&quot;,&quot;&lt;a href &#39;<a href="http://google.com" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://google.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792407289017000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nq1F58jxiVkFpalvLhsM_">http://google.com</a>&#39;&gt;google&lt;\a&gt;&quot;,&quot;&lt;/td&gt;&quot;, sep = &quot;&quot;)</div><div>        }</div><div>        str</div><div>    })</div><div><br></div><div>output$test_table_url2 &lt;-  renderTable(</div><div>    {</div><div>        tab1 = data.frame(x = c(&#39;a&#39;), y = c(&#39;&lt;a href=&quot;<a href="http://google.com" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://google.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792407289017000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nq1F58jxiVkFpalvLhsM_">http://google.com</a>&quot;&gt;google&lt;/a&gt;&#39;))</div><div>        tab1</div><div>    }, sanitize.text.function=function(x){x})</div><div>    </div><div>})</div></div><div><br></div>
